			<td class="textmode">202400104</td><td class="textmode">CRM</td><td class="textmode">CRM Operation</td><td class="textmode">25</td><td class="textmode">Root cause analysis for batch no. B0648489, defect - RP was not found to be effective. The department needs to strengthen the process of Root cause analysis</td><td class="textmode">Clause 10.2
When a nonconformity occurs, including any arising from complaints, the organization shall
a) react to the nonconformity and, as applicable
b) evaluate the need for action to eliminate the cause(s) of the nonconformity, in order that it does not
recur or occur elsewhere
c) implement any action needed
d) review the effectiveness of any corrective action taken
e) update risks and opportunities determined during planning, if necessary
f) make changes to the quality management system, if necessary</td><td class="textmode">&nbsp;</td><td class="textmode">&nbsp;</td><td class="textmode">Minor NC</td><td class="textmode">Again Root Cause analysis will be done .</td><td class="textmode">10-03-2024</td><td class="textmode">Again  root cause analysis has been done and CCA updated</td><td class="textmode">Root Cause  was not properly effective to  identify the problem</td><td class="textmode">06-03-2024</td><td class="textmode">Please review and update CCA</td><td class="textmode">OPEN</td>
		</tr><tr style="color:#000066;background-color:White;">
			<td class="textmode">202400105</td><td class="textmode">CRM</td><td class="textmode">CRM Operation</td><td class="textmode">25</td><td class="textmode">The process flow for Planning of changes is not effective. The department needs to be review the process flow and close the open loops in order to strengthen the system</td><td class="textmode">Clause 6.3
When the organization determines the need for changes to the quality management system, the changes
shall be carried out in a planned manner. 
The organization shall consider:
a) the purpose of the changes and their potential consequences;
b) the integrity of the quality management system;
c) the availability of resources;
d) the allocation or reallocation of responsibilities and authorities.
</td><td class="textmode">&nbsp;</td><td class="textmode">&nbsp;</td><td class="textmode">Minor NC</td><td class="textmode">Process flow of planning changes to be modified as per requirement.</td><td class="textmode">10-03-2024</td><td class="textmode">Process flow of planning changes has been modify as per requirement and amendment in DPM </td><td class="textmode">&nbsp;</td><td class="textmode">06-03-2024</td><td class="textmode">Evidence verified</td><td class="textmode">CLOSE</td>
